==Russian==

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|orv|азъбукы|tr=azъbuky}}, {{borrowing|cu|азъбоукꙑ|tr=azŭbuky|lang=ru}}, from the names of the first two letters of the Cyrillic alphabet, {{etyl|cu|ru}} {{compound|азъ|боукꙑ|tr1=azъ|tr2=buky|lang=cu|nocat=1}}, a [[calque]] of {{etyl|grc|ru}} {{term|ἀλφάβητος|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈazbʊkə/|lang=ru}}
* {{audio|Ru-а́збука.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|а́збука}}

# [[alphabet]]
#: {{ux|ru|[[азбука Морзе]]|Morse code|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[азбука Брайля]]|Braille|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[слоговой|слоговая]] азбука|syllabary|inline=1}}
# ABC book, [[abecedary]]; [[primer]]
# [[ABC]] {{gloss|the rudiments of any subject}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|а́збука}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|alphabet}} {{l|ru|алфавит}}
* {{sense|ABC book}} {{l|ru|букварь}}
* {{sense|the rudiments of any subject}} {{l|ru|основа|основы}}, {{l|ru|азы}}

